thanks, I tried to find but failed, to find Math::wrapi.

About being not a valid change, I accept your point of view - I'd argue that the computational complexity is minimized by the contents of the functions, it's easier to reason about this:

```
void EditorMainScreen::select_next() {
	select(_wrap_selection(1));
}
```

Than the original code.  and now there's a single point of failure instead of two.

The speed lost here is negligible as this is not in a hot path (even if it is, I'd argue that it would be negligible. the original code was not caching editor_table.size(), and this one is, reducing function calls (even if there is a newer function added).

I will update this to use Math::wrapi in a bit.

